{"term":"landmark","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:773153f26ccc6f27e1","definition":"An object that marks the boundary of a piece of land (usually a stone, or a tree).","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["merestone"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"historical","register":"historical","wordFamily":["interlandmark","landmarkable","landmark case","Landmarker","Landmarkism","Landmarkist","pseudolandmark","semilandmark"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/landmark#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8b7e69c5ac9428d1ec","definition":"A recognizable natural or man-made feature used for navigation.","example":"Anyone have any weird landmarks they often remember seeing along roads in the olden days?","pos":"noun","synonyms":["marker","mark"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["interlandmark","landmarkable","landmark case","Landmarker","Landmarkism","Landmarkist","pseudolandmark","semilandmark"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/landmark#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:64225187e8763fc5d5","definition":"A notable location with historical, cultural, or geographical significance.","example":"Founded in 1876 by disheartened gold prospectors, today downtown Rapid City is a mix of historic landmarks such as the 1928 Hotel Alex Johnson and the 1912 Elks Theatre, along with restaurants, coffee shops, specialty stores, boutiques and art galleries that reflect the busy modern city.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["monument","sight"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["interlandmark","landmarkable","landmark case","Landmarker","Landmarkism","Landmarkist","pseudolandmark","semilandmark"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUr